ents participate in **both** MATHCOUNTS and Science Club.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Use the principle of inclusion-exclusion\n\nLet:\n- $ M $ = number of students in MATHCOUNTS = 28\n- $ S $ = number of students in Science Club = 21\n- $ N $ = number of students in **neither** = 6\n- $ B $ = number of students in **both** MATHCOUNTS and Science Club (what we're solving for)\n\nWe know that:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total students} = M + S - B + \\text{Neither}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the known values:\n\n$$\n50 = 28 + 21 - B + 6\n$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\n50 = 55 - B\n$$\n\nSolve for $ B $:\n\n$$\nB = 55 - 50 = 5\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{5}\n$$\n\n**5 students participate in both MATHCOUNTS and Science Club.**", "diagnostic_seconds": 7.75847081374377}
